                        <p>However, every strength left unchecked can become a liability. Your drive to be successful at all costs can cause you to lose yourself in the process. Vulnerability does not come easy as you want to maintain the successful persona most people see you as. You begin to believe that you are only your accomplishments and nothing more which affects not only you but those closest to you. </p>
                        <p>In these moments of losing yourself in your striving you are constantly comparing yourself to others becoming even more competitive, self-promoting, and image conscious. Enter the risk of burnout as you believe you are only as good as your last accomplishment.</p>
                        <p>At your worst you think, “What does a successful me look like in your eyes?”</p>
                        <p>At your best you believe, “I am successful because of who I am, not what I do.” </p>
                        <p class='mb-0'>At your healthiest your confidence and enthusiasm is inspiring to others, you leverage this to bring out the best in those around you. You focus on others’ success over your own believing that serving a greater mission and purpose is the ultimate form of success. You use your adaptability, productivity, and drive for excellence for the greater good.</p>

                    ",
