                        <p>You experience the world as a naturally intrusive and overwhelming place. Believing that life demands too much of you, you focus your attention on conserving your energy and resources to avoid depletion. This intense desire to hoard resources and control your environment can become damaging to relationships as you can become extremely private and emotionally distant.</p>
                        <p>You often feel that you must know as much as possible before sharing your thoughts to avoid being seen as or feeling incompetent. This can overwhelm you and cause you to retreat.</p>
                        <p>This desire for knowledge, independence, and a life free from obligations can strain your relationships since connection, feelings, and vulnerability are natural components to a healthy partnership. The demands of living in relationship with others is overwhelming so you maintain a healthy distance so you are not easily obligated.</p>
