                    "s1_title" => "Always the optimist, others are drawn to your naturally encouraging energy. People are inspired by your limitless view of life.",
                    "s1_content" => "
                        <p>Externally you are positive and happy, internally, you are always wanting more and fearful of missing out on something. Life is like cotton candy, sweet to the taste, but disappears quickly. To avoid being left without you are always striving for more.</p>
                        <p>You experience a deep internal wrestling when life becomes difficult as you seek to avoid emotional pain. When life gets complicated, painful, sad, or boring, you quickly escape to things that please you, allowing you to avoid painful or negative experiences. The problem with pursuing adventure, happiness, and stimulating experiences is the inability to enjoy the and appreciate the present.</p>
                        <p>In avoiding these painful experiences you will often find you end up creating even more painful experiences down the road. Avoiding painful things, or reframing negative into positive without truly dealing with it will always show up in counterproductive ways throughout your life.</p>
                        <p>Becoming scattered, uncommitted, and unreliable may cause your relationships to suffer. People close to you may get frustrated when they feel you value new experiences and people more than them. These tendencies can hinder emotional depth such as walking through challenging experiences together.</p>
                        <p class='mb-0'>At your best, you embrace the present, able to savor it with gratitude. Trusting your needs will be met, you become more receptive and thoughtful. When you combine this with your natural creativity and energy, you’ll inspire others as you walk through both the highs and lows of life.</p>
