                    "s3_content" => "Wings are the Enneagram types that neighbor yours that add certain characteristics to your personality from those types. Typically, one wing is more dominant that the other, however, it is not uncommon for a person to have “balanced wings” where they take characteristics from each wing equally.",
                    "wing1_title" => "7w6 “Entertainer”",
                    "wing1_content" => "More anxious and slow to react than the 7w8. Still very adventurous yet more calculated in their decisions.",
                    "wing2_title" => "7w8 “Realist”",
                    "wing2_content" => "Entrepreneurial in nature. Seeks strength and power in pursuit of new external opportunities.",
                    "leadership_style_title" => "Leadership Style",
                    "leadership_style_strengths_title" => "Strengths",
                    "leadership_style_strengths_content" => "Starter, innovative, relational, outgoing, fun, energetic.",
                    "leadership_style_weaknesses_title" => "Weaknesses",
                    "leadership_style_weaknesses_content" => "Scattered, lack of focus, low follow-through, lack of empathy.",
                    "leadership_style_lead_title" => "How to lead Type 7s",
                    "leadership_style_lead_content" => "Type 7’s make great leaders but are not necessarily great managers. To lead is to create and that is what the Type 7 is best at. They will lead and find new exciting ways to accomplish a mission. To manage is to maintain and the idea of “maintenance” will eventually trigger the 7’s greatest fear of being trapped. If you let them run they will learn new ways to serve your mission and your team. This type will thrive in the brainstorm phase of any idea or project.",
                    "s4_title" => "Triads",
                    "s4_content" => "Your triad is another way of describing how you consistently interpret and respond to life. They are also known as the “Centers Of Intelligence” and are made up of three sets of three Enneagram types. Types 2, 3, and 4 are in the heart or feeling triad, types 5, 6, and 7 are in the head or thought triad, and types 8, 9, and 1 can be found in the gut or instinct triad.",
                    "s4_triads_img" => "/images/results/Enneagram_Diagram_Triads-5-6-7.png",
                    "triad_title" => "5,6,7 - Head / Thought",
                    "triad_subtitle" => "Emotional Struggle - Fear/Anxiety",
                    "triad_items" => [
                        "<b><span>5 -</span> Externalizes Fear -</b> Fearful of the anxiety caused by not knowing or having enough the Type 5 will seek to learn as much as possible and hoard their resources to avoid the fear of not having or knowing enough. This constant fear of lack leads to the dominant struggle of greed.",
                        "<b><span>6 -</span> Internalizes Fear -</b> Fearful of the anxiety caused by all of the worst possible outcomes the Type 6 will attempt to plan and prepare for all of these worst case scenarios in an attempt to manage their anxiety. However, it is impossible to predict all possible outcomes which will lead to the dominant struggle of crippling anxiety.",
                        "<b><span>7 -</span> Forgets Fear -</b> Fearful of the anxiety caused by their inner world the Type 7 will keep themselves busy with external stimulus, actions, and adventures to not have to face their internal fears and emotions. This constant seeking leads to the dominant struggle of gluttony."
                    ],
                    "triad_subtitle2" => "Common Desire: Security",
                    "triad_items2" => [
                        "<b><span>5 -</span> Seeks security through knowledge, stockpiling resources, or time alone -</b> The Type 5 is most attuned to their energy levels and will become more withdrawn or angry when they feel obligated or invaded.",
                        "<b><span>6 -</span> Seeks security in knowing and planning for all possible outcomes -</b> They will seek this same level of security from those around them and may become frustrated or anxious if they feel this security is threatened.",
                        "<b><span>7 -</span> Seeks security by avoiding their inner fears and looking to their external world to fill them up -</b> They will seek new adventures, experiences, and relationships to avoid having to be alone with their thoughts and emotions. If they feel trapped or limited they will seek an escape."
                    ],
                    "s5_title" => "Childhood Interpretations",
                    "s5_content" => "Childhood Interpretations tell us how our type perceives or interprets life starting in childhood. We often carry this interpretation into adulthood which can lead to unhealthy or self-defeating behavior. We believe that your situations and circumstances did not make you who you are but rather your interpretation and response to those situations and circumstances created a pattern of behavior in how you approach the world. We believe that we are born with our Enneagram type, we are uniquely created with this personality type and see the world through the lens of our individual personalities. Think back to your childhood and think about how you may have viewed the world through your childhood interpretation and how you can begin leveraging this understanding moving forward.",
                    "s5_box_title" => "Type 7",
                    "s5_box_content" => "“It’s not okay to depend on others for anything.”",
                    "s6_title" => "Defense Mechanisms",
                    "s6_content" => "Defense Mechanisms are our default method of dealing with stress or stressful situations.",
                    "s6_box_title" => "Type 7 - Rationalization",
                    "s6_box_content" => "
                        <p>Type 7s avoid owning their real intentions, motivations, and how their behavior impacts others by rationalizing their unacceptable thoughts, feelings, and actions.</p>
                        <p class='mb-0'>They are skilled at knowing how to reframe any situation so their behavior is justified. This allows them to avoid the reality of sadness, grief, hurting others, pain, limitations, or boredom. They are skilled masters at charming their way out of being in trouble by spinning any negative situation into one that sounds positive, fun, and exciting to others. They are so upbeat, positive, and likable that it is hard for others to stay angry or upset with them.</p>
                    ",
                    "s7_title" => "Interpersonal Relationships (AKA “Stances”)",
                    "s7_content" => "This shows us how we get others to respond to us to get our needs met. There are three different interpersonal styles; Assertive, Dutiful, and Withdrawn.",
