                    "subtitle" => "Protective, Confident, Assertive, Confrontational, Self-Forgetting, Intense",
                    "s1_title" => "Justice and protection are the fuel to your fire. You leverage your big-hearted nature and strength to be the change you want to see.",
                    "s1_content" => "
                        <p>In the same way you seek protection for others you also seek protection for yourself. Your tough exterior is to ensure you are not taken advantage of or manipulated. Betrayal is your greatest fear and yet you tend to believe it is inevitable so you fight to earn and build a trusting environment. </p>
                        <p>Your intense nature to achieve justice and control can often leave others in your wake. They will not be able to run as hard or understand your aggressive nature which often leads to you being misunderstood. You are acting in their and your best interest but not all people are wired like you, they just won’t understand. Your drive will be perceived as domineering, confrontational, and insensitive. Underneath your external strength is a deep fear of loss or betrayal and a heart that would do anything to serve those around them. This must be communicated vocally, however, because it is rarely felt. Where other people become fearful and passive, you face your fears head-on becoming aggressive. “I will control my fears before they control me.” </p>
                        <p>Inevitably, this approach ends up doing more harm than good. To protect yourself, you live in denial, suppressing your emotions that cause you to feel vulnerable, out of control or exposed, living as though those feelings never existed.</p>
                        <p>In relationships with others, you may sacrifice intimacy so that your weaknesses can’t be discovered and used against you. Denying yourself closeness and tenderness with others, as well as the giving or receiving of forgiveness, leaves you feeling incomplete. You miss out on the intimacy and support you actually long for. </p>
                        <p class='mb-0'>When you are at your best, you can surrender your fear of betrayal and need for control and allow people to see an endearing and compassionate strength. From that place, you can better protect the innocent from injustice, empower others, and use your leadership to accomplish your ultimate goals.</p>
                    ",
